  "body": "I don't like the idea of using critical CSS - it violates the separation between *markup* and *appearance*. So I expect `<link rel=\"preload\" as=\"style\">` to work like this because the word looks like to do BEFORE anything is loaded, but it loads CSS (and other sources) **AFTER** HTML file is loaded.\r\n\r\nSo I came up with an idea of an attribute value that tells browser **to download the file IMMEDIATELY when the `<link>` element was parsed**. I'd like to name it `rel=\"critical\"` because the term \"critical CSS\" is popular and it tells the *urgency* of the element very well.",
